{"id": 8356980, "full_name": "Brian T. Emmer", "first_name": "Brian T.", "last_name": "Emmer", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Interrogation_of_ACE2_modifiers_in_Calu-3_cells_/19287305", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>(A) FACS plots of ACE2 surface staining in Calu-3 cells treated with control nontargeting (NT) or <i>SMAD4</i>-targeting gRNA for each of 3 technical replicates. (B) Volcano plots of MAGeCK Robust Rank Aggregation scores and gene-level gRNA log<sub>2</sub> fold-change in ACE2<sup>negative</sup> relative to ACE2<sup>positive</sup> populations for each gene tested in the focused CRISPR library in Calu-3 cells. Genes with FDR <0.05 and absolute log<sub>2</sub> fold-change >1 are highlighted, with positive regulators in blue and negative regulators in red. (C) Comparison of log<sub>2</sub> fold-change in ACE2<sup>negative</sup> relative to ACE2<sup>positive</sup> populations in focused CRISPR screens of HuH7 (x-axis) and Calu-3 (y-axis). Only <i>ACE2</i>, highlighted in blue, was identified in both screens with FDR<0.05 and absolute log<sub>2</sub> fold-change >1. Genes identified as significant in only the HuH7 or Calu-3 screens are highlighted in magenta and red, respectively. (D) Immunoblotting of lysates collected from Calu-3 cells targeted by CRISPR with a gRNA against the indicated gene or a nontargeting (NT) control sequence. (E) Percentage of cells with detectable surface ACE2 staining after CRISPR-mediated single gene disruption of the indicated target gene or a nontargeting control in Calu-3 cells. Candidate genes associated with positive or negative regulation of ACE2 in the CRISPR screen are highlighted in blue and red, respectively. ACE2-positive gates were defined on control unstained cells and the proportion of ACE2-positive cells for each population is displayed for each of 3\u20136 technical replicates. Error bars depict standard deviation. Asterisks indicate p<0.05 by Student\u2019s t-test. Source data and statistical analysis are provided in <a href=\"http://www.plospathogens.org/article/info:doi/10.1371/journal.ppat.1010377#ppat.1010377.s018\" target=\"_blank\">S9 Table</a>.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 655248, "created_date": "2022-03-01T18:39:56Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-11T16:29:39Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["viral spike protein", "throughput crispr screens", "suggest potential targets", "influence cellular susceptibility", "immortalized cell lines", "established transcription factors", "cell type specificity", "3 cells revealed", "host factors involved", "derived huh7 cells", "div >< p", "ace2 regulatory networks", "ace2 modifiers comprised", "ace2 surface abundance", "host cells", "surface abundance", "functional networks", "functional modifiers", "derived calu", "regulate ace2", "ace2 regulators", "ace2 expression", "ace2 </", "vivo </", "ugp2 </", "smad4 </", "report high", "pias1 </", "orthogonal screening", "mrna level", "molecular pathways", "mogs </", "kdm6a </", "gpaa1 </", "findings clarify", "epigenetic regulators", "ep300 </", "enriched among", "distinct set", "bambi </", "2 infection", "2 entry"], "keywords": ["viral spike protein", "throughput crispr screens", "suggest potential targets", "influence cellular susceptibility", "immortalized cell lines", "established transcription factors", "cell type specificity", "3 cells revealed", "host factors involved", "derived huh7 cells", "div >< p", "ace2 regulatory networks", "ace2 modifiers comprised", "ace2 surface abundance", "host cells", "surface abundance", "functional networks", "functional modifiers", "derived calu", "regulate ace2", "ace2 regulators"